{#
   Plain text, not markup.

   A password link is the one message this application sends, and it is the
   message an attacker most wants to imitate. A plain-text email has no hidden
   link targets, no images that report when it was opened, and no styling that
   can make one address look like another — a reader can see exactly where the
   link goes, which is the only defence against a convincing copy of this message.
#}
Hello {{ displayName }},

Somebody asked to set a new password for your account on {{ site_name }}.

Open this link to choose one:

{{ link }}

The link works once and lasts an hour.

If it was not you, nothing has happened to your account and you can ignore this
message — your current password still works.
